/T (A dive bar date an anniversary doth not make)
/E (A dive bar date an anniversary doth not make)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
339 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 200 0 R
/E (I decided to take the wife out for a night on the town for our anniversary this week. She often likes me to plan these sorts of things -- I believe she sees the effort I expend in the planning department as an expression of love and care. Seeing as this wasn't just any ordinary date, but an anniversary occasion, I decided to pull out the big guns.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
340 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 200 0 R
/E (We've been having fun with Texas two step dancing lately and through extensive research I discovered a place in Austin that was playing live music on a Tuesday night and thought I had a winner. Keep in mind the key feature of this bar was that it played dance music, I was not necessarily interested in other aspects of the establishment \(my wife would later say that I did not pay attention to such aspects\).)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
341 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 200 0 R
/E (The odd thing about this bar was that it wasn't really in a commercial area. I had to do a doubletake when I was looking up directions because it's kinda in a weird residential neighborhood behind some strip malls and box stores. Nevertheless, we departed for our date.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
342 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 200 0 R
/E (Things seemed like they were looking up when we pulled into the pitted, dusty gravel parking lot: the yard had more plastic lawn chairs than grass and the building was kind of broken down \(the front door looked like it wasn't in the frame right and there was a big handpainted piece of cardboard that said 'Danger! Use back door!"\) and the rusted metal roof was covered in spray paint -- but the spray paint was actually quite nice, depicting antlers and the bar's name in fancy print. These are usually signs of a good honky tonk place.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 200 0 R
/E (Upon entering this fine establishment, we were confronted with a lonesome man playing an electric guitar in a manner that seemed tired although I suppose he meant it to be soulful. We later determined that he was part of a musical duo the other half of which was not in attendance due to some mishaps with a raccoon or armadillo or something.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
344 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 200 0 R
/E (We groped our way through the very dim interior to the bar to order drinks I discovered that they had a Square terminal.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
345 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 200 0 R
/T (A brief aside)
/E (A brief aside)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
346 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 200 0 R
/E (I've been looking for Square terminals most of the places I go this year. Unfortunately, I rarely find them. Instead, I see all these other payment processors with names that can only be described as overly cozy. Normally, I'm not the kind of person who tries to orange pill or to preach the good orange word to others. But I've been getting hyped up by all you people with your stories of spending sats and such and I think I let the excitement of being able pay for our date with sats get the better of me.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
347 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 200 0 R
/T (Diving in)
/E (Diving in)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
348 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 200 0 R
/E (We ordered margaritas from a woman who's exterior perfectly suited the building and went to sit down. We headed toward a very comfortable-looking corner table but ended up at a different table because upon closer inspection it seemed that someone had taken a knife \(or perhaps a machete or chainsaw or something\) to the upholstery of the black leather bench.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
349 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 200 0 R
/E (After we found a seat, a mournful dog came over and put her head in my wife's lap. I think she \(my wife, not the dog\) was startled by this and perhaps desired that I keep the animal from doing this. I did push it away some and she \(the dog, not my wife\) came and laid her head in my lap instead. The dog was incredibly reluctant to move elsewhere, despite my best efforts to shove it's head off my lap.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [19]
>>
endobj
350 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 200 0 R
/E (It was at this point that we noticed the ceiling. It was one of those false ceilings like you might see in a cheap office or something, but it had the unique appearance of being a thousand years old. pieces of some sort of dirty cloth were hanging from it in very dramatic tatters and in other places it had been completely gouged away to reveal the dark interior of the attic area.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [20]
>>
endobj
351 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 200 0 R
/E (When you looked across the bar at the stage, the ceiling gave the distinct impression of being on the verge of collapsing. The area above the musician was certainly several feet lower than where we were -- unless the man was a giant of some sort.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [21]
>>
endobj
352 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 200 0 R
/E (Then my wife began sneezing. In the course of the next ten minutes, she experienced an incredibly strong allergy attack. I kept her supplied with paper towels to blow her nose \(the bar did not provide napkins\) but it didn't seem to do much good.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
353 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 200 0 R
/E (I began to enjoy myself, sipping a margarita and listening to the blues which, if it wasn't Two Step music nor even terribly good, at least embodied the concept of the genre. Unfortunately, my wife's sneezing continued to get worse and we had to leave.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
